.el .ds Aq '
.TH sealtask 1  "SealTask CLI 0.2.1" "SealTask Manual"
.SH NAME
sealtask \- CLI for working with SealTask tasks, comments, notes, attachments, and decrypted workspace data
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsealtask\fR [\fB\-\-api\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-storage\-origin\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-progress\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-v \fR]... [\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-\-connect\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-read\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-request\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-retry\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
CLI for working with SealTask tasks, comments, notes, attachments, and decrypted workspace data
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH CONNECTION
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-url\fR \fI<API_URL>\fR [default: https://sealtask.com]
SealTask API base URL
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_API_URL\fR environment variable.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-storage\-origin\fR \fI<STORAGE_ORIGIN>\fR
Trusted origin for presigned attachment transfers (repeatable)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_STORAGE_ORIGINS\fR environment variable.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-connect\-timeout\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR
Maximum time to establish a control\-plane connection (for example 5s)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_CONNECT_TIMEOUT\fR environment variable.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-read\-timeout\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR
Maximum idle time while reading a control\-plane response (for example 30s)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_READ_TIMEOUT\fR environment variable.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-request\-timeout\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR
Maximum total time for one control\-plane request (for example 1m)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_REQUEST_TIMEOUT\fR environment variable.
.RE
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit compact JSON instead of human\-readable output
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Select human\-readable, finite JSON, or streaming JSON Lines output
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
json\-pretty
.IP \(bu 2
jsonl
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Control colors in human\-readable output
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_COLOR\fR environment variable.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-pager\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Control paging of long human\-readable output
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_PAGER_MODE\fR environment variable.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Disable paging (equivalent to \-\-pager never)
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Control delayed progress indicators on stderr
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_PROGRESS\fR environment variable.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress automatic paging, progress, and successful mutation acknowledgements
.SH INTERACTION
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; fail with an actionable validation error when input is missing
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Emit redacted operator telemetry to stderr; repeat for more detail
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Emit maximum redacted diagnostic telemetry to stderr
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-retry\fR \fI<COUNT>\fR [default: 2]
Retry replay\-safe API requests after transient failures
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_RETRY\fR environment variable.
.RE
.SH PROFILE
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Isolate credentials and unlock state under a named profile
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_PROFILE\fR environment variable.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Override the base directory used for credentials and local unlock state
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_CONFIG_DIR\fR environment variable.
.RE
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
sealtask\-completion(1)
Generate a shell completion script without reading configuration or credentials
.TP
sealtask\-man(1)
Render a manual page for the root command or a nested command path
.TP
sealtask\-info(1)
Show machine\-readable CLI capabilities and contract versions
.TP
sealtask\-schema(1)
Describe commands and arguments as human help or versioned JSON
.TP
sealtask\-auth(1)
Authenticate, inspect the session, and manage local unlock state
.TP
sealtask\-me(1)
Show the current authenticated user
.TP
sealtask\-pick(1)
Fuzzy\-pick an entity while printing only a reusable opaque selector
.TP
sealtask\-projects(1)
List, inspect, select, archive, or restore projects
.TP
sealtask\-tasks(1)
List, inspect, create, update, move, or delete tasks
.TP
sealtask\-stats(1)
Show current dashboard task counts
.TP
sealtask\-activity(1)
Inspect or continuously follow recent account activity
.TP
sealtask\-batch(1)
Validate, execute, and safely resume task mutations from JSON Lines
.TP
sealtask\-doctor(1)
Diagnose local state, authentication, unlock, and API connectivity
.TP
sealtask\-config(1)
Inspect resolved operator configuration
.TP
sealtask\-profile(1)
List profiles or change the persisted default profile
.TP
sealtask\-comments(1)
List, create, update, or delete task comments
.TP
sealtask\-notes(1)
List, inspect, create, update, or delete encrypted notes
.SH EXTRA
Get started:
  sealtask auth login
  sealtask auth status
  sealtask projects list
  sealtask tasks list \-\-all

Run \*(Aqsealtask help <command>\*(Aq for command\-specific help.
.SH VERSION
v0.2.1
